      "name": "Jawahar",
      "created_at": "2026-02-18T05:07:05.204Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hello everyone,</p>\n<p>Our company uses Tally to manage accounting data. Currently, we export the records from Tally and manually import them into the ERPNext application.</p>\n<p>We want to automate this process and sync Tally records directly with ERPNext.</p>\n<p>Is there any way to achieve automatic synchronization? Are there any tools available for this purpose?</p>\n<p><a class=\"hashtag-cooked\" href=\"/tag/frappe\" data-type=\"tag\" data-slug=\"frappe\" data-id=\"96\" data-style-type=\"icon\" data-icon=\"tag\"><span class=\"hashtag-icon-placeholder\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-square-full svg-icon svg-node\"><use href=\"#square-full\"></use></svg></span><span>frappe</span></a> <a class=\"hashtag-cooked\" href=\"/c/erpnext/6\" data-type=\"category\" data-slug=\"erpnext\" data-id=\"6\" data-style-type=\"square\"><span class=\"hashtag-icon-placeholder\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-square-full svg-icon svg-node\"><use href=\"#square-full\"></use></svg></span><span>ERPNext</span></a> <a class=\"hashtag-cooked\" href=\"/c/erpnext/accounts/7\" data-type=\"category\" data-slug=\"accounts\" data-id=\"7\" data-style-type=\"square\" data-ref=\"erpnext:accounts\"><span class=\"hashtag-icon-placeholder\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-square-full svg-icon svg-node\"><use href=\"#square-full\"></use></svg></span><span>ERPNext &gt; Accounting</span></a> <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#tally</span></p>\n<p><a class=\"hashtag-cooked\" href=\"/c/integration/27\" data-type=\"category\" data-slug=\"integration\" data-id=\"27\" data-style-type=\"square\"><span class=\"hashtag-icon-placeholder\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-square-full svg-icon svg-node\"><use href=\"#square-full\"></use></svg></span><span>Integration</span></a> <a class=\"hashtag-cooked\" href=\"/tag/chart_of_accounts\" data-type=\"tag\" data-slug=\"chart_of_accounts\" data-id=\"232\" data-style-type=\"icon\" data-icon=\"tag\"><span class=\"hashtag-icon-placeholder\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon