    {
      "id": 496430,
      "username": "senguttuvang",
      "name": "SenG",
      "created_at": "2026-03-26T15:52:45.233Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Tally to ERPNext may not be viable path ever. Tally doesn’t export their jounal entries, only the statements/exports. Don’t have API. Rather, you directly post the entries from your bank and other sources to ERP Next. You may either ask the accountant to sync ERP Next entries to Tally, manually. You may consider this tool (<a href=\"https://github.com/PearlThoughts/LedgerBridge\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">GitHub - PearlThoughts/LedgerBridge: Bank statement to beancount bookkeeping automation for Indian businesses. The missing middleware between raw financial data and cloud accounting. · GitHub</a>) to post to ERP Next with ease.</p>\n<p>You may consider phasing out Tally. Consider ERP Next as your primary system and use Zohobooks or another modern accounting system that offers API which can satisfy your needs of keeping all the systems in sync</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/6bbea6/{size}.png",
